CMTypes/Algebra.lean
--------------------
New file (70f2e46): algebraic background for CM types. Line numbers as
of 2026-10-02 (commit 45007ad).
[x] Algebra ℚ (center R)                                             (l.18–47)
      SMul, center_algebra_map and the Algebra instance are done.

[x] IsCentral_basechange, IsCentral_basechange'                      (l.58, l.170)
      Base change of a central algebra is central. Done (45007ad), two
      proofs: the long one over a K-basis of F, and a short one via
      Subalgebra.centralizer_range_includeRight_eq_center_tensorProduct.
      Could keep only the short one.

[ ] IsSimpleRing_basechange                                          (l.190)
      F ⊗[K] R is simple. Has [IsCentral K R] (false without it:
      ℂ ⊗[ℝ] ℂ ≅ ℂ × ℂ). Not in Mathlib. Started: a nonzero x ∈ J is
      obtained; the rest is sorry (l.205).
      A complete ~55-line proof was worked out (2026-10-02) but not
      inserted:
        - φ := TensorProduct.equivFinsuppOfBasisLeft (chooseBasis K F);
          φ((1⊗r)x) i = r * φ x i and φ(x(1⊗r)) i = φ x i * r;
        - pick x ∈ I, x ≠ 0, with minimal (φ x).support.card (Nat.find);
        - the i₀-coefficients of elements of I supported in supp x form
          a TwoSidedIdeal of R (TwoSidedIdeal.mk'), so contain 1
          (IsSimpleRing.one_mem_of_ne_zero_mem): get y with φ y i₀ = 1;
        - by minimality (1⊗r)y = y(1⊗r), so y is central, so
          y = algebraMap F _ f (IsCentral_basechange'), f ≠ 0;
        - (f⁻¹⊗1)·y = 1 ∈ I, so I = ⊤ (TwoSidedIdeal.eq_top).

[ ] fact₁ / dimension_IsSimple_algebra                               (l.215, l.228)
      Proved modulo IsSimpleRing_basechange; both carry [IsCentral K R].
      finrank K R = n * n should follow via Module.finrank_baseChange;
      the reduced degree could then be defined directly as
      Nat.sqrt (finrank K R) instead of via choose.

[ ] Cleanup: remove the trailing `#min_imports` and the commented-out
      `--#check IsSimpleRing.isField_center` (l.56).


